{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/482399-enjoy-and-critique-my-unholy-house-rules","id":482399,"title":"Enjoy (and Critique) my Unholy House Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-16T08:28:43-07:00","id":482399,"title":"Enjoy (and Critique) my Unholy House Rules","content":"Enjoy (and critique, constructively, should you feel inspired) my unholy house rules for my Vampire Dark Ages campaign, with ideas liberally ripped off from Requiem 2e. I stopped short of making vampires sparkly, but made some hacks to support &quot;dark, brooding, vampire (anti) super-heroes&quot; mode. Joking aside, if you see anything for which you have a better mechanical hack, feel free to share!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cUm1AcObyJmfgRlAfniACJ31osSjkDdUfIIvsRDlRJg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cUm1AcObyJmfgRlAfniACJ31osSjkDdUfIIvsRDlRJg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cUm1AcObyJmfgRlAfniACJ31osSjkDdUfIIvsRDlRJg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cUm1AcObyJmfgRlAfniACJ31osSjkDdUfIIvsRDlRJg/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:49:25-07:00","id":482645,"title":"","content":"Overall I respect some of what you're trying to do. Though I'm not a big fan of Requiem, Blood Potency is a much better system than Gen. However, I can't support it being ported into Masquerade. The idea of Generation is just too intrinsic to the setting to be removed without drastically rewriting the setting material.<br /> <br /> Languages I'd suggest going to the V20 system. It's much better than the Linguistics skill. Language is just a 1 point merit that can be bought for 1fb or 3xp in game. Far smoother.I like the idea, particularly in DA though of giving bonus starting languages.<br /> <br /> I don't at all like limiting the blood bond to only affecting Willpower 5 or less. It way too severely weakens the power of the blood bond, which particularly in Dark Ages was the elders' most potent and pervasive means of control. This very thing is what caused the resentment that sparked the Anarch Revolt. Without it, the setting would be a VASTLY different place.<br /> <br /> I think you'd be better off working the questions you have in Heightened Senses into Auspex 2. They seem far more in theme with Aura Perception.<br /> <br /> Cutting the Paths and Roads, again particularly in Dark Ages so severely limits roleplay as to make the game almost non-functional. The average mortal in the Dark Ages couldn't have maintained a humanity above maybe 4 (and as noted, most didn't, usually favouring Road of Kings or Road of Heaven), much less vampires. The Path of Humanity is just insufficient to portray life in the Middle Ages. Those simply were not the values of society at the time, and as such it makes no sense to force it. <br /> <br /> There's my $.02 at least. Take it as you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:05:56-07:00","id":482759,"title":"","content":"Good advice killersquirrel59. I will do the following:<br /> <br /> - use V20 languages<br /> - i need to reword the blood bond thing. It affects everyone, you just only get the creepy &quot;i'm deeply in love with you&quot; think with weak willed people. They're still bonded in the sense that they are devoted to and supportive. The romantic part of the blood bond just is to wierd for me. That's a personal feeling.<br /> - auspex 1 -&gt; auspex 2<br /> - I'll have to clarify the humanity thing. It should be a set of breaking points that are appropriate to the time and place. I'll clean that up.<br /> <br /> Great advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T16:19:22-07:00","id":482905,"title":"","content":"That makes more sense on the blood bond thing. <br /> <br /> On the humanity subject, the problem is that the values of society are not universal. They are wildly different depending on era and culture. A single path of Humanity is just not sufficient to ever really cover it all. This is far more the case in Dark Ages when cultures were far more isolated. A Norseman who properly should be following the Via Einherjar or the Via Aesirgard has very little in common morally with say an Italian merchant following the Via Mercator. Coming up with a universal 10 point system is just very unlikely to work. And that's just mortals. The issue is 100 times worse with Cainites who can come from any era, not to mention the added change just from being a vampire. I can barely comprehend how even a modern vampire can sustain Humanity above maybe 3-4 as described in the Core Book. I usually run my world that most vampires over 100 years old are on some alternate Path, though the Camarilla takes pains to hide this, as they are still trumpeting the propaganda that all should follow Humanity, since it makes its members more controllable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}